- Use of oral isotretinoin must be permanently discontinued for at least 2 weeks prior to consideration date (confirmed by the prescribing physician) and;
- Eye evaluation must be done in accordance with specifications in 8500-7 and;
- The airman must provide a signed statement of discontinuation that: - Confirms the absence of any visual disturbances and psychiatric symptoms, and - Acknowledges requirement to notify the FAA and obtain clearance prior to performing any aviation safety-related duties if use of isotretinoin is resumed
